.TH PARALLEL-EXEC 1 "2026-02-21" "ShellScript Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
parallel-exec \- execute commands in parallel with rate limiting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B parallel-exec
[\fImax-jobs\fR]
.PP
or read commands from stdin:
.PP
cat commands.txt | \fBparallel-exec\fR [\fImax-jobs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Executes shell commands in parallel while respecting a maximum
number of concurrent jobs. Useful for batch processing, scraping,
distribution, and any task that can be parallelized.
.PP
Waits for all jobs to complete before exiting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B max-jobs
Maximum concurrent processes (default: 4)
.SH EXAMPLES
.B cat urls.txt | parallel-exec 5
Runs 5 downloads simultaneously from urls.txt
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xargs (1),
.BR parallel (1) (GNU parallel)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Fabbio for ShellScript Toolkit Pro
